sed from the point $(0, 3)$ to the point $(3, 0)$, as shown above?\n\n*Hint: Use the parametrization $r(t) = ⟨3\\cos t, 3\\sin t⟩$.*"] [17592186134082 :question/problem "![](images/f5/f531f2467284ef84e0af0758a8e8554f1e5f72ea08d30d0b80c83076fbe5d7a3.png)\n\nEvaluate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}(x+\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi y)\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$ where $C$ is the path traversed along the line segment from the point $(1,0)$ to the point $(2,1),$ as shown above."] [17592186134083 :question/problem "![](images/36/36b985c811eb28d8220017c6b7407b3a104554d785dafdb35f17553c262bdc35.png)\n\nWhich of the following is equivalent to $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}xy\\,\\text{d}y,\n$$ where $C$ is the path along the line segment from the point $(-1,-2)$ to the point $(2,4),$ as shown above?\n\n*Hint: Use the parametrization $r(t)=⟨3t-1,\\,6t-2⟩.$*"] [17592186134084 :question/problem "![](images/84/8417d2d62e9213ec3f92108495107fc982dc399e52cca8982e01516457f5692a.png)\n\nEvaluate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}\\frac{2y}{x}\\,\\text{d}y,\n$$ where $C$ is the path along the upper-right quarter of the ellipse $9{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}=36,$ traversed from the point $(2,0)$ to the point $(0,3),$ as shown above."] [17592186134085 :question/problem "![](images/1b/1b693165c8f6201e96f0a972746324c65a308d1f143f229c465b6aa22b7aeb16.png)\n\nWhich of the following is equivalent to $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}(x-y)\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$ where $C$ is the path along the ellipse $16{x}^{2}+25{y}^{2}=400,$ traversed from the point $(0,-4)$ to the point $(5,0),$ as shown above?\n*Hint: Use the parametrization $r(t)=⟨5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩.$*"] [17592186134086 :question/problem "![](images/f8/f83043b44a8ad9181e66de57357397deb49c4b0e79b5e6e16330305a58391148.png)\n\nWhich of the following is equivalent to $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}xy\\,\\text{d}y,\n$$ where $C$ is the path along a circle of radius $4,$ traversed from the point $(4,0)$ to the point $(-4,0),$ as shown above?\n\n