 \\\\ ↓ & ↓ \\\\ 142, 800 & \\div\\end{vmatrix}400\n$$\n\nSo we need to find the value of $142,800 \\div 400$, which we can write as the following fraction:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{142,800}{400}\n$$\n\nDividing the numerator and denominator by $100$, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{142,800 \\div 100}{400 \\div 100} = \\dfrac{1,428}{4}\n$$\n\nwhich is the same as $1,428 \\div 4$.\n\nComputing the quotient, we obtain:\n\n| $\\,\\, {\\:\\phantom{\\mid} {\\:\\phantom{\\mid}} 3 {\\:\\phantom{\\mid}} 5 {\\:\\phantom{\\mid}} 7}$$4$$\\!\\enclose{longdiv}{1 {\\:\\phantom{\\mid}} 4 {\\:\\phantom{\\mid}} 2 {\\:\\phantom{\\mid}} 8}$$-\\!\\!\\!$$1$$2$$2$$2$$-\\!\\!\\!$$2$$0$$2$$8$$-\\!\\!\\!$$2$$8$$0$ |\n| --- |\n\nTherefore, $142,773 \\div 398$ is approximately $357$."] [17592186138276 :question/worked-solution "First, we round both numbers to the nearest whole number:\n$$\n\\displaystyle 539.5\\begin{vmatrix}\\div & 18.2 \\\\ ↓ & ↓ \\\\ 540 & \\div\\end{vmatrix}18\n$$\nSo, we need to find the value of $540 \\div 18$. Using long division, we get:\n\n| $3$$0$$18$$\\!\\!\\enclose{longdiv}{5 {\\:\\phantom{\\mid}} 4 {\\;\\phantom{\\mid}} 0}$$-\\!\\!\\!\\!$$5$$4$$0$$0$ |\n| --- |\n\nThat is,\n\n$$\n540 \\div 18 = 30\n$$\n\nTherefore, $539.5 \\div 18.2$ is approximately $30$."] [17592186138306 :question/problem "Consider the following functions:\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle f(x)=8-x, \\qquad g(x)=\\sqrt[3]{50x}\n$$\n\nBy filling the empty cells in the table below, find an approximate solution to $f(x)=g(x)$.\n\n| $x$ | $2.5$ | $2.6$ | $2.7$ | $2.8$ | $2.9$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $f(x)$ |  | $5.4$ |  |  | $5.1$ |\n| $g(x)$ |  | $5.07$ |  |  | $5.25$ |\n| $f(x) - g(x)$ |  | $0.33$ |  |  | $-0.15$ |\n| $\\mid f(x)-g(x) \\mid$ |  | $0.33$ |  |  | $0.15$ |"] [17592186138307 :question/problem "![](images/d1/d1e168bdbd8d02a5cf4b18bbeb6cd5a30aa2089e7a3dca274b5ef4c53efc2b74.png)\n\nUsing the graph, find an approximate solution to the system of equations below.\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle {\\left\\{